IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (NSW) -- Parts 1 and 2: who is a public official, what serious wrongdoing is,
-- and whether a disclosure is a public interest disclosure, and of which kind (ss 13, 14, 20-29, Dictionary).
--
-- SEAT: the public official who makes, or is thinking of making, a disclosure about serious wrongdoing (the discloser).
-- Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Am I a public official?", "Is what I am reporting serious
-- wrongdoing?", "Is my disclosure a public interest disclosure, and of what kind?", "From what day may I go to a member
-- of Parliament or a journalist?". Agencies, integrity agencies, the Ombudsman, Ministers and courts get no seat.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "only if" or "unless", a flat "is not"), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 30 October 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 -- Parts 1 and 2`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 14(1) "public official means 1 or more of the following" -- paragraphs (a) to (i), in order.
DECLARE `My position` IS ONE OF
    `I am employed in or by an agency, or otherwise in its service`
    `I have public official functions that an integrity agency is authorised to investigate`
    `I am an individual in the service of the Crown`
    `I am a statutory officer`
    `I provide services or exercise functions for an agency, including as a contractor, subcontractor or volunteer`
    `I work for an entity engaged to provide services or exercise functions for an agency, and am involved in that work`
    `I am a judicial officer`
    `I am a member of Parliament or a Minister`
    `I am employed under the Members of Parliament Staff Act 2013`
    `none of these`

-- s 14(2): the regulations may declare a person to be, or not to be, a public official. The Public Interest
-- Disclosures Regulation 2022 is not deposited, so what it says is asked.
DECLARE `What the regulations say about me` IS ONE OF
    `the regulations say nothing about me`
    `the regulations declare me to be a public official`
    `the regulations declare me not to be a public official`

-- s 13 "serious wrongdoing means 1 or more of the following", with the Dictionary's definitions of paragraphs (b)-(e).
-- "Corrupt conduct" has the meaning in the Independent Commission Against Corruption Act 1988 (a borrowed term, asked).
DECLARE `What my disclosure is about` IS ONE OF
    `corrupt conduct`
    `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts`
    `a contravention of a pecuniary interest obligation under the Local Government Act 1993 or a council code of conduct`
    `administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives`
    `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts`
    `a serious and substantial waste of public money`
    `something else`

-- How the disclosure came to be made: ss 22 (witness), 23 (mandatory; a code of conduct is not a legal obligation,
-- s 23(2)), and otherwise of the maker's own accord (voluntary, s 24).
DECLARE `How I came to make the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `of my own accord`
    `because a code of conduct told me to`
    `in meeting the ordinary requirements of my role or functions`
    `under a statutory or other legal obligation`
    `at the request of, or as required by, someone investigating serious wrongdoing`

-- s 27(1) recipients, (a)-(e), and anyone else. s 27(2): written correspondence sent to an agency's usual address and
-- not addressed to anyone is made to the head of the agency.
DECLARE `To whom I made the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `the head of an agency`
    `another disclosure officer for an agency`
    `my manager`
    `a Minister or a member of a Minister's staff`
    `a member of Parliament who is not a Minister`
    `a journalist`
    `someone else`

-- The answer to "what kind of public interest disclosure is mine?" (ss 21, 22, 23, 24, 29).
DECLARE `The kind of disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `a voluntary public interest disclosure`
    `a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency`
    `a witness public interest disclosure`
    `a mandatory public interest disclosure`
    `not a public interest disclosure`

§§ `s 14 -- am I a public official`

-- s 14(1) is a "means" definition: no paragraph met is JUST FALSE. s 14(2) regulations declare in or out.
@export Am I a public official under the NSW Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 14)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position` @desc Your position. One of: "I am employed in or by an agency, or otherwise in its service", "I have public official functions that an integrity agency is authorised to investigate", "I am an individual in the service of the Crown", "I am a statutory officer", "I provide services or exercise functions for an agency, including as a contractor, subcontractor or volunteer", "I work for an entity engaged to provide services or exercise functions for an agency, and am involved in that work", "I am a judicial officer", "I am a member of Parliament or a Minister", "I am employed under the Members of Parliament Staff Act 2013", "none of these". An agency includes a Public Service agency, the NSW Police Force, the Teaching Service, NSW Health Service, a council, a State owned corporation and an integrity agency (s 16)
      `what the regulations say` IS A `What the regulations say about me` @desc Whether the Public Interest Disclosures Regulation declares you to be, or not to be, a public official. One of: "the regulations say nothing about me", "the regulations declare me to be a public official", "the regulations declare me not to be a public official"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a public official` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the regulations say`
    WHEN `the regulations declare me not to be a public official` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the regulations declare me to be a public official` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `my position` EQUALS `none of these`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 13 and the Dictionary -- serious wrongdoing`

-- The Dictionary excludes "a trivial failure" from a government information contravention and a privacy contravention,
-- and "conduct of a trivial nature" from serious maladministration. s 20(2): a disclosure may be about serious
-- wrongdoing whether or not it occurred, so the question is what the disclosure alleges or tends to show.
@export Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing under the NSW Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 13 and the Dictionary)?
GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What my disclosure is about` @desc What your disclosure alleges or tends to show. One of: "corrupt conduct" (as the ICAC Act defines it), "a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts" (the GIPA Act, the GIIC Act or the State Records Act 1998), "a contravention of a pecuniary interest obligation under the Local Government Act 1993 or a council code of conduct", "administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives", "a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts" (PPIP Act 1998 or HRIP Act 2002), "a serious and substantial waste of public money", "something else"
      `it is trivial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure or conduct is trivial (this matters only for the information, privacy and maladministration kinds)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what it is about`
    WHEN `something else` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts` THEN JUST (NOT `it is trivial`)
    WHEN `administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives` THEN JUST (NOT `it is trivial`)
    WHEN `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts` THEN JUST (NOT `it is trivial`)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What my disclosure is about`, `it is trivial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is about serious wrongdoing` `what it is about` `it is trivial` IF
    `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `what it is about` `it is trivial` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 26 -- content of a voluntary public interest disclosure`

-- s 26(1) complies "if the maker ... honestly, and on reasonable grounds, believes the disclosure shows or tends to show
-- serious wrongdoing" (the honesty of the belief is presumed from the maker's indication, s 26(5); asked as a fact).
-- s 26(2) not if "relates only to a disagreement with a government policy". s 26(3) not if "concerns only a grievance
-- about ... employment" and either has no significant implications beyond the individual or relates to a disagreement
-- with reasonable management action; s 26(4) unless the grievance arises from a decision on, or alleged detrimental
-- action over, a previous voluntary public interest disclosure.
GIVEN `I believe it shows serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is only a disagreement with government policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is only an employment grievance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grievance has significant implications beyond the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grievance is a disagreement with reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grievance arises from an earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure complies with section 26` IF
        `I believe it shows serious wrongdoing`
    AND (NOT `it is only a disagreement with government policy`)
    AND (NOT `section 26(3) excludes it`)
    WHERE
        DECIDE `section 26(3) excludes it` IF
                `it is only an employment grievance`
            AND (   (NOT `the grievance has significant implications beyond the individual`)
                 OR `the grievance is a disagreement with reasonable management action`)
            AND (NOT `the grievance arises from an earlier disclosure`)

§§ `s 28 -- disclosures to a member of Parliament or a journalist`

-- s 28(2) "investigation period ... means (a) the period of 6 months from the making of the previous disclosure, or (b)
-- if the maker ... applies within 6 months ... for internal review ... the period of 12 months". Fork F1 for the end day.
GIVEN `the day of the earlier disclosure` IS A DATE, `I applied for internal review within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the investigation period` `the day of the earlier disclosure` `I applied for internal review within 6 months` MEANS
    IF `I applied for internal review within 6 months`
    THEN `the day of the earlier disclosure` `plus months` 12
    ELSE `the day of the earlier disclosure` `plus months` 6

-- s 28(1)(e)(i) "has not, at the end of the investigation period, received ... the required information": that can be
-- true only once the period has ended, so the first day on which it can be met is the day after its last day.
@export If an agency has not told me the outcome of my earlier disclosure, from what day may I take it to a member of Parliament or a journalist (s 28(1)(e)(i), (2))?
GIVEN `the day of my earlier disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made substantially the same disclosure to the head of an agency, a disclosure officer, your manager, or a Minister or Minister's staff member
      `I applied for internal review within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within 6 months of that earlier disclosure, you applied for internal review of an agency decision about it (this stretches the period to 12 months)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` MEANS
    (`the last day of the investigation period` `the day of my earlier disclosure` `I applied for internal review within 6 months`) `plus days` 1

-- s 28(1) "only if, in addition to complying with sections 25-27": (a) substantially true; (b) substantially the same
-- voluntary public interest disclosure made earlier to a person in s 27(1)(a)-(d); (c) the earlier one not anonymous;
-- (d) no written waiver of the right to information under s 59; (e) either (i) the required information not received at
-- the end of the investigation period, or (ii) notified at any time of a decision in s 55(3) (neither to investigate nor
-- refer, or to stop investigating without completing or referring). "Only if" closes the list: a failed condition is
-- JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `it is substantially true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made substantially the same disclosure earlier to a proper recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier disclosure was anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I waived in writing my right to information about the earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was told of a decision not to investigate or refer, or to stop investigating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I received the required information by the end of the investigation period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the earlier disclosure` IS A DATE
      `I applied for internal review within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of this disclosure` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 28 conditions are met` IF
        `it is substantially true`
    AND `I made substantially the same disclosure earlier to a proper recipient`
    AND (NOT `the earlier disclosure was anonymous`)
    AND (NOT `I waived in writing my right to information about the earlier disclosure`)
    AND (   `I was told of a decision not to investigate or refer, or to stop investigating`
         OR (    `the day of this disclosure` `is after` (`the last day of the investigation period` `the day of the earlier disclosure` `I applied for internal review within 6 months`)
             AND (NOT `I received the required information by the end of the investigation period`)))

§§ `ss 21-29 -- what kind of public interest disclosure`

-- s 23(1) mandatory: about serious wrongdoing, made by a public official (a) while meeting the ordinary requirements of
-- the role or (b) under a statutory or other legal obligation (not a code of conduct, s 23(2)).
-- s 22 witness: in an investigation of serious wrongdoing, at the request or requirement of the investigator; not if
-- mandatory (s 22(2)).
-- s 24(1)(a) voluntary: complies with s 25 (a public official who is not a member of Parliament), s 26 (content) and
-- s 27 (recipient); s 28 adds conditions for a member of Parliament or journalist; s 24(3) not if witness, mandatory, or
-- made orally to a Minister or a Minister's staff.
-- s 24(1)(b), s 29: a written determination by the head of an agency makes it voluntary "even if the disclosure would
-- not otherwise be"; a revocation (s 29(8)) has effect from the time the determination was made (s 29(9)). Fork F2: the
-- determination does not override s 24(3)(a)-(b) (a witness or mandatory disclosure stays what it is, and is a public
-- interest disclosure anyway), and it overrides s 21(2) until revoked.
-- s 21(2) "a disclosure is not a public interest disclosure to the extent that the maker ... wilfully makes a false
-- statement to, or misleads or attempts to mislead" the recipient. Fork F3: read as the whole disclosure.
@export What kind of public interest disclosure did I make, if any, under the NSW Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (ss 21-29)?
GIVEN `I was a public official when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a public official when you made the disclosure (see the question "Am I a public official")
      `I am a member of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of Parliament (including a Minister)
      `what it is about` IS A `What my disclosure is about` @desc What your disclosure alleges or tends to show. One of: "corrupt conduct", "a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts", "a contravention of a pecuniary interest obligation under the Local Government Act 1993 or a council code of conduct", "administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives", "a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts", "a serious and substantial waste of public money", "something else"
      `it is trivial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure or conduct you report is trivial (matters only for the information, privacy and maladministration kinds)
      `how I came to make it` IS A `How I came to make the disclosure` @desc How you came to make it. One of: "of my own accord", "because a code of conduct told me to", "in meeting the ordinary requirements of my role or functions", "under a statutory or other legal obligation" (including a manager's duty to pass on a disclosure), "at the request of, or as required by, someone investigating serious wrongdoing"
      `I believe it shows serious wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you honestly believe, on reasonable grounds, that the disclosure shows or tends to show serious wrongdoing
      `it is only a disagreement with government policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information relates only to a disagreement with a government policy (including spending decisions or a council's policy)
      `it is only an employment grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information concerns only a grievance about someone's employment or former employment
      `the grievance has significant implications beyond the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that grievance has significant implications beyond matters personally affecting the individual
      `the grievance is a disagreement with reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that grievance relates to a disagreement with reasonable management action taken or proposed
      `the grievance arises from an earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grievance arises from an agency's decision on an earlier voluntary public interest disclosure, or from alleged detrimental action over one
      `to whom I made it` IS A `To whom I made the disclosure` @desc To whom you made it. One of: "the head of an agency" (including a letter or email to an agency's usual address not addressed to a person), "another disclosure officer for an agency", "my manager", "a Minister or a member of a Minister's staff", "a member of Parliament who is not a Minister", "a journalist", "someone else"
      `I made it orally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it by speaking rather than in writing
      `it is substantially true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether the disclosure is substantially true
      `I made substantially the same disclosure earlier to a proper recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether you earlier made substantially the same voluntary public interest disclosure to the head of an agency, a disclosure officer, your manager, or a Minister or Minister's staff member
      `the earlier disclosure was anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether that earlier disclosure was anonymous (there was no reasonably practicable way to communicate with you about it)
      `I waived in writing my right to information about the earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether you waived in writing your right to be kept informed about the earlier disclosure
      `I was told of a decision not to investigate or refer, or to stop investigating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether an agency told you it had decided neither to investigate nor to refer the earlier disclosure, or to stop investigating without completing or referring it
      `I received the required information by the end of the investigation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether, by the end of the 6 (or 12) month investigation period, an agency had given you notice of its decision to investigate, a description of the results, and details of corrective action
      `the day of the earlier disclosure` IS A DATE @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: the day you made the earlier disclosure
      `I applied for internal review within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a member of Parliament or journalist only: whether you applied for internal review of an agency decision about the earlier disclosure within 6 months of making it
      `the day of this disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made this disclosure
      `I wilfully made a false statement or misled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in making the disclosure, you wilfully made a false statement to, or misled or tried to mislead, the person you made it to
      `the head of an agency determined it is voluntary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the head of an agency has determined in writing that your disclosure is a voluntary public interest disclosure (s 29)
      `that determination was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that determination has been revoked
GIVETH A `The kind of disclosure`
`What kind of public interest disclosure did I make` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is mandatory` AND (NOT `I wilfully made a false statement or misled`) THEN `a mandatory public interest disclosure`
           IF `it is a witness disclosure` AND (NOT `I wilfully made a false statement or misled`) THEN `a witness public interest disclosure`
           IF `it is mandatory` OR `it is a witness disclosure` THEN `not a public interest disclosure`
           IF `the head of an agency determined it is voluntary` AND (NOT `that determination was revoked`) THEN `a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency`
           IF `I wilfully made a false statement or misled` THEN `not a public interest disclosure`
           IF `it meets sections 24 to 28` THEN `a voluntary public interest disclosure`
           OTHERWISE `not a public interest disclosure`
    WHERE
        DECIDE `it is mandatory` IF
                `I was a public official when I made it`
            AND `the disclosure is about serious wrongdoing` `what it is about` `it is trivial`
            AND (   `how I came to make it` EQUALS `in meeting the ordinary requirements of my role or functions`
                 OR `how I came to make it` EQUALS `under a statutory or other legal obligation`)
        DECIDE `it is a witness disclosure` IF
            `how I came to make it` EQUALS `at the request of, or as required by, someone investigating serious wrongdoing`
        DECIDE `it goes to a member of Parliament or a journalist` IF
               `to whom I made it` EQUALS `a member of Parliament who is not a Minister`
            OR `to whom I made it` EQUALS `a journalist`
        DECIDE `it meets sections 24 to 28` IF
                `I was a public official when I made it`
            AND (NOT `I am a member of Parliament`)
            AND `the disclosure complies with section 26` `I believe it shows serious wrongdoing` `it is only a disagreement with government policy` `it is only an employment grievance` `the grievance has significant implications beyond the individual` `the grievance is a disagreement with reasonable management action` `the grievance arises from an earlier disclosure`
            AND (NOT (`to whom I made it` EQUALS `someone else`))
            AND (NOT (`to whom I made it` EQUALS `a Minister or a member of a Minister's staff` AND `I made it orally`))
            AND (   (NOT `it goes to a member of Parliament or a journalist`)
                 OR `the section 28 conditions are met` `it is substantially true` `I made substantially the same disclosure earlier to a proper recipient` `the earlier disclosure was anonymous` `I waived in writing my right to information about the earlier disclosure` `I was told of a decision not to investigate or refer, or to stop investigating` `I received the required information by the end of the investigation period` `the day of the earlier disclosure` `I applied for internal review within 6 months` `the day of this disclosure`)

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `The kind of disclosure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a public interest disclosure` `the kind` IF (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `not a public interest disclosure`))

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `The kind of disclosure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a voluntary public interest disclosure` `the kind` IF
       `the kind` EQUALS `a voluntary public interest disclosure`
    OR `the kind` EQUALS `a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency`
